---
import Answer from "../../components/challenge/Answer.astro";
import ChallengeIntro from "../../components/challenge/ChallengeIntro.astro";
import Checklist from "../../components/challenge/Checklist.astro";
import Message from "../../components/challenge/Message.astro";
import Task from "../../components/challenge/Task.astro";
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Debug from an Email - AI Training Guide">
	<PageShell chapterId="exploring-ai-capabilities" subChapterId="debug-from-email">
		<ChallengeIntro skill="You can hand the agent a bad photo of an error and let it find the page, the steps to reproduce, and the fix.">
			A policyholder hit an error in the consumer portal. Support forwarded their email, and the only detail is a phone photo of
			their monitor.
		</ChallengeIntro>

		<Message
			kind="email"
			subject="Fwd: error on my bill"
			from="Kaiju Mutual Support"
			to="Web Team"
			date="Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:12"
			attachments={[{ name: "IMG_4471.jpg", href: "/downloads/kaiju-mutual/4.billing-receipt-error.jpg" }]}
		>
			<p>I tried to view my bill and got this error.</p>
		</Message>

		<Task>Write a prompt to have your agent find the page in the photo, reproduce the error, and fix it.</Task>

		<Checklist
			items={[
				"Work out which page the photo shows.",
				"Reproduce the error in the browser before changing any code.",
				"Explain which click, on which data, causes it.",
				"Fix the cause so the same kind of bug can't come back.",
				"Confirm the fix in the browser.",
			]}
		/>

		<Answer
			prompt={`A customer sent this photo of an error in the consumer portal: <image>

Work out which page it is and what they clicked to get there. Reproduce it with agent-browser before changing anything, then fix the cause, not just the symptom, and confirm the fix in the browser.`}
		>
			<p>
				The photo shows the URL and the error, so finding the page is easy. The work is finding the click. The error appears
				after <strong>Billing</strong>, the <strong>⋯</strong> menu on a payment, then <strong>View receipt</strong>, and only on
				the refunded payment. The other rows open fine.
			</p>
			<p>
				The error screen says "Couldn't load this page", which reads like a failed request. There's no request ID on it, which is
				the first clue that it isn't one: it's a render error. The receipt's wording is looked up by payment status, and nobody
				added an entry for <code>Refunded</code>.
			</p>
			<p>
				A good agent signs in, opens the menu and tries rows in agent-browser until one breaks. If it only read the code and
				grepped for <code>title</code>, ask it to confirm in the browser.
			</p>
			<p>
				Adding a <code>Refunded</code> entry fixes the symptom. The fix worth seeing types the lookup with{" "}
				<code>satisfies Record&lt;PaymentStatus, …&gt;</code>, the way <code>statusVariant</code> in the same file already
				is, so the compiler catches the next status someone forgets.
			</p>
		</Answer>
	</PageShell>
</MainLayout>
